# Wiki Schema — {{project_name}}

This file governs how the project's wiki works. Every orchestrator (/compile, /audit) reads this before doing anything. It documents the directory structure, file formats, routing rules, and lifecycle conventions for the compounding-knowledge pipeline shipped by the `knowledge-os` capability.

---

## 1. Wiki Structure

The project's configured wiki domains:

{{wiki_domains_table}}

Directory tree (assumed when `knowledge-os` is enabled and `wiki_domains` is populated):

```
project-root/
├── raw/                    # Append-only intake. Never edited after creation.
├── wiki/                   # Compiled knowledge articles, organized by domain
│   ├── INDEX.md            # Top-level index across all domains
│   ├── HEALTH.md           # Coverage/staleness snapshot, regenerated by /compile
│   ├── REVIEW.md           # Issue tracker for items needing operator attention
│   └── <domain>/           # One subdirectory per declared wiki_domain
│       └── INDEX.md        # Per-domain index, regenerated by /compile
├── roadmap/                # Phase-by-phase build articles with assumption tables
│   └── INDEX.md
├── references/             # Reference material (vendor docs, external specs)
│   └── README.md           # Catalog of reference material
├── receipts/               # One file per orchestrator run, machine-consumed
├── changelog.md            # Human-readable run log — companion to receipts/ (see § 7)
└── SESSION-BRIEFING.md     # Single-file onboarding for new sessions
```

**Empty-state convention for unpopulated `wiki_domains`:** When `project.yaml.wiki_domains` is empty (initial state, before the INIT.md walkthrough populates it), the wiki-domains table above renders as the literal text "(No domains declared yet — populate during INIT.md walkthrough.)" and `/compile` refuses to route raw files. Operators must declare at least one domain before knowledge intake can begin.

