## 5. Roadmap Articles (`roadmap/`)

Roadmap articles track build phases and their assumptions. Each phase has its own article.

```markdown
---
title: Phase name
phase: 0 | 1 | 2 | 3 | ...
status: active | completed | blocked | future
last_updated: 2026-05-15
---

# Phase N — Name

## Summary

What this phase delivers and why it matters.

## Assumptions

Every assumption that must hold for this phase to succeed.

| # | Assumption | Type | Status | Evidence | Wiki Source |
|---|------------|------|--------|----------|-------------|
| 1 | <Specific testable claim>    | binary | confirmed | <Quote or measurement>           | wiki/<domain>/<article>.md |
| 2 | <Threshold claim>            | threshold | unvalidated | <Estimate, no hard data>     | — |
| 3 | <Spectrum claim>             | continuous | at-risk | <Signal description>          | wiki/<domain>/<article>.md |

## Blockers

Active blockers. Link to `roadmap/blockers.md` for cross-phase blockers if that file exists.

## Dependencies

What must be done before this phase starts.
```

### Assumption Types

| Type | Meaning | How /audit checks it |
|------|---------|----------------------|
| `binary` | True or false. | Direct evidence in wiki → confirmed / refuted / unvalidated. |
| `continuous` | Lives on a spectrum (high/medium/low or partial/at-risk/mostly-confirmed). | Aggregate signals in wiki → rate position on spectrum. |
| `threshold` | Has a critical value ("we need at least X"). | Find measured value, compare to threshold. |

The `Type`, `Status`, `Evidence`, and `Wiki Source` columns are **machine-walked** — graded by `/audit` and updated by `/compile`'s roadmap cascade — so keep the table shape exact. This table defines the assumption *types*; the full per-type grading protocols (status vocabularies, transition rules, REVIEW-entry triggers) live in the `/audit` skill (`.claude/skills/audit/SKILL.md`).

