## 8. REVIEW.md Schema

`wiki/REVIEW.md` is the wiki's issue tracker.

### Entry Format

```markdown
### [TYPE] Short description

- **Severity:** blocking | standard | background
- **Created:** 2026-05-15
- **Stale after:** 2026-05-18 (blocking=3d) | 2026-05-22 (standard=7d) | 2026-05-29 (background=14d)
- **Source:** /compile run 2026-05-15 (or /audit, etc.)
- **Details:** What needs attention and why.
- **Resolution:** (filled when resolved)
```

### Review Types

| Type | Created by | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| `compile` | `/compile` | Circuit breaker hit — N articles remain unprocessed |
| `audit` | `/audit` | Phase 2 assumption #3 has no wiki evidence |
| `connection` | `/compile` (deferred to future `/discover`) | Cross-link uncertainty — operator decides |
| `cascade` | `/compile` | Roadmap phase 1 assumption changed — downstream may be affected |
| `correction` | `/compile` | Personnel correction conflicts with existing source — needs resolution |
| `scale` | any | Threshold crossed (article count, REVIEW queue size) |
| `routing` | `/compile` | Raw file's tags do not match any declared wiki domain |

### Severity and Staleness

| Severity | Staleness window | Meaning |
|----------|------------------|---------|
| `blocking` | 3 days | Blocks a build phase or corrupts data if ignored |
| `standard` | 7 days | Should be addressed but doesn't block progress |
| `background` | 14 days | Nice to resolve, low urgency |

### Resolution Statuses

The `Resolution:` field, once filled, carries one of these statuses. They split into **terminal** (the work is done) and **deferred** (a future condition is named). This split is the line `/compile` Step 6a sweeps on (§ 12 Lifecycle): terminal entries are deleted every compile; deferred entries are preserved because they are not done.

| Status | Class | Meaning |
|--------|-------|---------|
| `APPLIED` | terminal | The fix was made. |
| `WONT-FIX` | terminal | Decided not to act; closed. |
| `SUPERSEDED` | terminal | Replaced by a newer entry or decision. |
| `RESOLVED` | terminal | Otherwise settled; nothing left to do. |
| `DUPLICATE` | terminal | Same issue tracked elsewhere. |
| `DEFERRED`-until-X | deferred | Parked behind a named future condition X; re-opens when X fires. |
| `ACCEPTED-UNCERTAINTY` | deferred | Low-stakes disagreement accepted, carrying a re-open trigger (see § 13). |

An entry with no `Resolution:` filled is simply **unresolved** (not a resolution status) — it counts toward the ~30-unresolved scale cap and is never swept. **If in doubt whether a resolution is terminal, leave it — preserve beats premature deletion.**

