## 9. HEALTH.md Schema

`wiki/HEALTH.md` is regenerated by `/compile`. Machine-readable snapshot.

```markdown
# Wiki Health

**Last updated:** 2026-05-15T14:30:00
**Total articles:** N
**Total raw inputs:** M
**Unprocessed raw:** K

## Coverage by Domain

| Domain | Articles | Avg Confidence | Oldest Update | Gaps |
|--------|----------|----------------|---------------|------|
| <domain-a> | N | high | 2026-05-10 | 2 |
| <domain-b> | N | medium | 2026-05-08 | 4 |

## Staleness Alerts

- wiki/<domain>/<article>.md — last updated 2026-05-01 (14 days)

## REVIEW.md Summary

- Blocking: N
- Standard: N
- Background: N
- Stale: N
```

The Coverage by Domain table carries one row per declared `wiki_domain` — regenerate the full set every run, including domains with zero articles. Dropping a domain's row is a Directory Preservation violation (§ 6). When a corpus binding is declared (`corpus_source` or `corpus_sources`), HEALTH.md also hosts the **§ Corpus Observation** table (one row per ground-truth source, keyed by corpus `id`, with its own last-reconciled SHA and last-observation status) — see § 16.

