## 10. SESSION-BRIEFING.md Format

Single-file onboarding for any new session — the fastest path to context. Regenerated by `/compile` after every run AND by `/flight-plan` at session start (its single write exception).

```markdown
# Session Briefing

**Last compiled:** YYYY-MM-DD
**Governing documents:** CLAUDE.md (governance), core/methodology/ (methodology kernel), this wiki's INDEX

## Architectural Context

3-4 paragraph summary of the project's architectural thesis. What is being built, the strategic frame, the load-bearing constraints. Not the full thesis — just enough that a cold session understands the frame. Link to the full thesis article for depth.

## Active Workstreams

### [Workstream Name]
- **Phase:** Which roadmap phase
- **Status:** One sentence — what was last done, what's next
- **Hold points:** Any active hold points blocking progress
- **Key docs:** Links to the 1-2 wiki articles most relevant to this workstream
- **Last activity:** Date of most recent raw file or compile touching this workstream

## Hold Points

Consolidated list of all active hold points across workstreams.

## Governance Reminders

Bullet list of the governance rules that sessions most commonly need.

## Quick Reference

| Resource | Location | What it is |
|----------|----------|------------|
| CLAUDE.md | CLAUDE.md | Project governance |
| Wiki Schema | docs/wiki-schema.md | This file |
| REVIEW.md | wiki/REVIEW.md | Open issues and action items |
| HEALTH.md | wiki/HEALTH.md | Wiki coverage and staleness stats |
| Handoffs Index | handoffs/INDEX.md | Substrate-separation inquiries |
```

**This is a derived projection — regenerated from scratch, never appended to.** Its sources (wiki state, receipts, HEALTH/REVIEW) stay single-writer-owned; if the projection ever disagrees with its sources, **the sources win.**

**Section-level carry-forward (authoring discipline, not a format change).** "Regenerated" means the output reflects current state — and when a section's inputs are unchanged since the last refresh, its current state *is* the existing text. Carry such sections forward verbatim instead of re-deriving them; rewrite only the sections whose inputs changed this run. This is still full regeneration — the writer affirms every section against current state — and it is never appending: stale text may never survive an input change.

The file should be readable in under 90 seconds. If it exceeds ~150 lines, summarize more aggressively.

